{
  "contract": "hmd-relay-wire",
  "version": 1,
  "about": [
    "Wire-protocol fixtures for the hmd relay, shared by every party that speaks it.",
    "Relay side: relay/test/contract.spec.ts (the real Worker + Durable Object) and relay/scripts/__tests__/contract-fixtures.test.mjs (the JS crypto and envelope codec).",
    "hmd side: test/relay-contract-fixtures.test.sh replays this file against bin/heimdall-relay-client with no network.",
    "$name in a string is a binding (see `bindings`). A value the relay mints (ids, codes, tokens, clocks) is matched by pattern when the relay is the producer, and takes its example when a client is fed it. A `computed` binding is derived from vectors.json by each consumer, so no key ever sits in this file.",
    "Everything a client or the phone sends is replayed byte for byte: JSON is serialized compact with the key order stored here.",
    "Sealed frames in `frames` are sealed under the session key HKDF(ECDH(hmdSeedHex, phnSeedHex)) with salt = bindings.session_id.example, sender tags hmd\\0 / phn\\0, nonce = tag + seq (8 bytes, big endian). hmd frames' plaintext is serialized with sorted keys (what the client does); phone frames' in the app's insertion order.",
    "Every state frame's plaintext also carries hmd's capability tokens in-band (zero-lag Ask 5): {\"caps\":[\"controls-v1\",\"dash-v1\",\"login-v1\",\"push-v1\",\"resync\",\"view-v1\",\"z-zlib\"],\"state\":{...}}. Keys are sorted, so caps is stored before state; acks carry no caps. login-v1 (remote Claude Code login) is listed whenever hmd loaded its login module, so it is part of the sealed bytes. controls-v1 (the phone's remote controls: interrupt, save-checkpoint, hook-toggle, fallback-mode) is listed whenever hmd loaded its controls module, so it is part of the sealed bytes too. push-v1 says hmd takes the phone's register_push / unregister_push / app_state commands (push notifications, PN2); hmd leaves it out when the operator sets HMD_PUSH=0, so this fixture is hmd with push on. view-v1 (the phone's read-only file diff, bin/lib/companion_view.py) is listed whenever hmd loaded that module, so it too is part of the sealed bytes. dash-v1 (custom dashboards: the phone's sealed dashboard-request and state.dashboards, bin/lib/companion_dashboards.py) is listed whenever hmd loaded that module, so it is part of the sealed bytes too. dash-alert-v1 (threshold alerts on number tiles, bin/lib/dashboard_alerts.py; requires dash-v1) and push-tile-alert-v1 (the push kind tile_alert that module registers into bin/lib/companion_push.py) are listed whenever hmd loaded them, so they are part of the sealed bytes too.",
    "POST /frames carries Connection: keep-alive: hmd keeps one persistent HTTP/1.1 connection per sender (state frames on one, acks on the other), so a replay counts requests, not connections.",
    "ack_non_increasing_seq is hmd's answer when command_send_message (seq 1) arrives again after hmd took seq 3: the replay guard refuses a device seq that is not above the last one it accepted and, because the frame opens under the session key, refuses it with this sealed ack -- ok false, detail non-increasing-seq, last the last device seq accepted (3), of_seq the replayed seq (1), no other key -- so the phone can seal the command again above last. It is hmd's fifth frame (seq 5). The replay re-sends command_send_message's wire byte for byte, so the fixture holds no second phone frame; a frame that does not open is never answered.",
    "The relay routes by URL and never reads envelope.session_id, so these sealed frames carry the fixture's session id, not the live one the relay minted.",
    "hmd's leg has two transports on ONE route, negotiated by the request alone. `stream` is the original chunked NDJSON response, what any client that sends no Upgrade header gets, and what an older relay answers an Upgrade request with (it ignores the header: status 200, content-type application/x-ndjson). `stream_ws` is the same route with `Upgrade: websocket`: a hibernatable WebSocket, so an idle session lets the Durable Object sleep. Every message on it is one envelope, the bytes of an NDJSON line without its newline; the relay never writes a keepalive there (hmd sends the text message `ping`, the runtime answers `pong` without waking the object).",
    "stream_ws.request.headers are exactly what bin/heimdall-relay-client sends, Sec-WebSocket-Key pinned to RFC 6455 section 1.3's sample so the replay is deterministic; the relay suite sends them too but can only assert the status, because the Sec-WebSocket-Accept header is added by the platform, not by the Worker. stream_ws.frames are the exact octets of the two messages that are not envelopes, in RFC 6455 framing: hmd's masked `ping` (mask pinned) and the relay's unmasked `pong`."
  ],
  "bindings": {
    "session_id": {
      "match": "^[0-9a-f]{8}-[0-9a-f]{4}-[0-9a-f]{4}-[0-9a-f]{4}-[0-9a-f]{12}$",
      "example": "ef5a2950-611b-4c1b-9e6c-96cbed2c0815"
    },
    "pairing_code": {
      "match": "^[A-Z2-7]{26}$",
      "example": "ABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZ"
    },
    "relay_session_token": {
      "match": "^[A-Za-z0-9_-]{43}$",
      "example": "FIXTUREnotASecretFIXTUREnotASecretFIXTUREno"
    },
    "device_token": {
      "match": "^[A-Za-z0-9_-]+\\.[A-Za-z0-9_-]{43}$",
      "example": "FIXTUREnotASecretFIXTUREnotASecret.FIXTUREnotASecretFIXTUREnotASecretFIXTUREno"
    },
    "epoch_seconds": {
      "match": "^[0-9]{10}$",
      "type": "integer",
      "example": 1790000000
    },
    "relay_url": {
      "example": "https://relay.example"
    },
    "ws_key": {
      "match": "^[A-Za-z0-9+/]{22}==$",
      "example": "dGhlIHNhbXBsZSBub25jZQ=="
    },
    "ws_accept": {
      "match": "^[A-Za-z0-9+/]{27}=$",
      "example": "s3pPLMBiTxaQ9kYGzzhZRbK+xOo="
    },
    "device_pubkey": {
      "computed": "device_pubkey_b64url"
    },
    "hmd_pubkey": {
      "computed": "hmd_pubkey_b64"
    }
  },
  "pair_init": {
    "request": {
      "method": "POST",
      "path": "/pair/init",
      "headers": {
        "Content-Length": "0"
      },
      "body": ""
    },
    "response": {
      "status": 200,
      "content_type": "application/json",
      "body": {
        "session_id": "$session_id",
        "pairing_code": "$pairing_code",
        "relay_session_token": "$relay_session_token",
        "exp": "$epoch_seconds"
      }
    },
    "qr": {
      "v": 1,
      "relay": "$relay_url",
      "session_id": "$session_id",
      "pairing_code": "$pairing_code",
      "exp": "$epoch_seconds",
      "hmd_pubkey": "$hmd_pubkey"
    }
  },
  "stream": {
    "request": {
      "method": "GET",
      "path": "/session/$session_id/stream",
      "headers": {
        "Authorization": "Bearer $relay_session_token"
      }
    },
    "response": {
      "status": 200,
      "content_type": "application/x-ndjson"
    },
    "lines": {
      "device_bound": {
        "v": 1,
        "session_id": "$session_id",
        "seq": 0,
        "sender": "relay",
        "type": "device_bound",
        "nonce": null,
        "ciphertext": null,
        "payload": {
          "device_pubkey": "$device_pubkey",
          "bound_at": "$epoch_seconds",
          "via": "qr"
        }
      },
      "keepalive": {
        "v": 1,
        "session_id": "$session_id",
        "seq": 0,
        "sender": "relay",
        "type": "keepalive",
        "nonce": null,
        "ciphertext": null,
        "payload": {
          "ts": "$epoch_seconds"
        }
      }
    }
  },
  "stream_ws": {
    "request": {
      "method": "GET",
      "path": "/session/$session_id/stream",
      "headers": {
        "Authorization": "Bearer $relay_session_token",
        "Upgrade": "websocket",
        "Connection": "Upgrade",
        "Sec-WebSocket-Key": "$ws_key",
        "Sec-WebSocket-Version": "13"
      }
    },
    "response": {
      "status": 101,
      "headers": {
        "Upgrade": "websocket",
        "Connection": "Upgrade",
        "Sec-WebSocket-Accept": "$ws_accept"
      }
    },
    "messages": {
      "device_bound": {
        "v": 1,
        "session_id": "$session_id",
        "seq": 0,
        "sender": "relay",
        "type": "device_bound",
        "nonce": null,
        "ciphertext": null,
        "payload": {
          "device_pubkey": "$device_pubkey",
          "bound_at": "$epoch_seconds",
          "via": "qr"
        }
      },
      "client_ping": "ping",
      "relay_pong": "pong"
    },
    "frames": {
      "client_ping": {
        "mask": "37fa213d",
        "hex": "818437fa213d47934f5a"
      },
      "relay_pong": {
        "hex": "8104706f6e67"
      }
    },
    "close_codes": {
      "session_ended": 4001,
      "superseded": 4002,
      "message_too_big": 1009
    }
  },
  "phone": {
    "claim": {
      "path": "/session/$session_id/ws",
      "query": {
        "pairing_code": "$pairing_code",
        "device_pubkey": "$device_pubkey"
      },
      "headers": {
        "Upgrade": "websocket"
      },
      "status": 101
    },
    "device_bound": {
      "v": 1,
      "session_id": "$session_id",
      "seq": 0,
      "sender": "relay",
      "type": "device_bound",
      "nonce": null,
      "ciphertext": null,
      "payload": {
        "device_token": "$device_token",
        "exp": "$epoch_seconds"
      }
    },
    "revoked": {
      "session_ended": {
        "v": 1,
        "session_id": "$session_id",
        "seq": 0,
        "sender": "relay",
        "type": "session_ended",
        "nonce": null,
        "ciphertext": null,
        "payload": {
          "reason": "revoked"
        }
      },
      "close_code": 4001,
      "late_claim_status": 410
    }
  },
  "frames_post": {
    "request": {
      "method": "POST",
      "path": "/session/$session_id/frames",
      "headers": {
        "Authorization": "Bearer $relay_session_token",
        "Content-Type": "application/json",
        "Connection": "keep-alive"
      }
    },
    "response_delivered": {
      "status": 200,
      "body": {
        "ok": true,
        "delivered": true
      }
    },
    "response_undelivered": {
      "status": 200,
      "body": {
        "ok": true,
        "delivered": false
      }
    }
  },
  "revoke": {
    "request": {
      "method": "POST",
      "path": "/session/$session_id/revoke",
      "headers": {
        "Authorization": "Bearer $relay_session_token",
        "Content-Length": "0"
      },
      "body": ""
    },
    "response": {
      "status": 200,
      "body": {
        "ok": true
      }
    }
  },
